  "notes": [
    "Top-level 'config' is the default config (from tests/unit/test_whitelabel.py::_cfg). A case may override only forbidden_terms via input.config.",
    "Expected outcome: 'pass' (text returned unchanged) or 'blocked' (a forbidden-term error). display_name returns '<brand_prefix> <family_names[family] or family> <size_suffixes[size_key] or size_key>' and then runs the same gate.",
    "Matching rule (corrected, R3): case-insensitive; a forbidden term is split into tokens on whitespace, '_' and '-'; tokens may be joined in the text by any run of [\\s_-]* (including zero characters); a match must begin on a token boundary (preceding character is not [A-Za-z0-9]). Hence 'CloudVPS', 'Cloud-VPS', 'cloud_vps' and 'Storage  VPS' are blocked, while '120i' does not hit the term '20i'.",
    "The three forbidden-term inputs 'Powered by ...', 'Cloud VPS 10', 'Buy our CONTABO plan' are blocked under both the archived and corrected rule.",
    "The archived scan_repo() file-walk is not exported (it had no tests, review R3). The port's CI/lint gate must be specified separately and must fail when it scans zero files.",
    "Provider names appear in this file only because they are the forbidden terms / blocked inputs under test; this file is internal test data and must never be shipped to customers."
  ],
